        <mxCell id="n16" value="Issue booking confirmation (not a readiness record) [W05-S01, W05-S04]" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="222" width="180" height="44" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e21" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;fontSize=9;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n3" target="n16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note1" value="UNCERTAIN: no source names who produces the clarification Intake needs, or by when [W05-S03]" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fdf1f1;strokeColor=#b03a3a;fontSize=9;dashed=1;align=left;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="710" y="594" width="300" height="42" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e22" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;strokeColor=#b03a3a;dashed=1;endArrow=none;" edge="1" parent="1" source="note1" target="n13"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note2" value="&lt;b&gt;Incident path [W05-S04]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;booking request recorded &amp;#8594; held slot recorded &amp;#8594; booking confirmation issued &amp;#8594; visitor arrives &amp;#8594; Intake displays held &amp;#8594; exception review. The path never reaches &quot;Record readiness for appointment&quot;. No completed readiness decision appears in the supplied trace before arrival; absence from the trace does not prove the decision never happened, so it is recorded as uncertainty." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fdf1f1;strokeColor=#b03a3a;fontSize=9;dashed=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="190" y="668" width="430" height="66" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="Scope and Findings" id="w05-findings">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1100" dy="800" grid="1" gridSize="10" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="Week 5 | Scope and Findings" style="text;html=1;fontSize=24;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#183c43;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="25" width="1070" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="scope" value="&lt;b&gt;1 · Process scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Matthew Le. Purpose: show how Cedar Junction's appointment work runs today, from request to the intake handoff. Start: a visitor requests an appointment [W05-S01]. End: Intake passes the visitor to the next staff team [W05-S03]. Roles modeled as lanes: Visitor, Scheduling, Clinical Operations, Intake, Next staff team. Outside the diagram: clinical care after the handoff, system or software design, and any change I would recommend. This model records current work only." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="78" width="1070" height="86" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="walkthrough" value="&lt;b&gt;2 · Check the two paths&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Ordinary appointment:&lt;/b&gt; request [W05-S01] &amp;#8594; record slot and support preferences &amp;#8594; booking details complete (Yes) &amp;#8594; request readiness &amp;#8594; Clinical Operations checks room and clinician [W05-S02] &amp;#8594; available (Yes) &amp;#8594; readiness recorded &amp;#8594; visitor arrives &amp;#8594; Intake finds status ready [W05-S03] &amp;#8594; support arrangements confirmed &amp;#8594; handoff to the next staff team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Incident appointment [W05-S04]:&lt;/b&gt; booking request recorded &amp;#8594; held slot recorded &amp;#8594; booking confirmation issued &amp;#8594; visitor arrives &amp;#8594; Intake displays held &amp;#8594; Dana opens exception review. The path never reaches Record readiness for appointment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;The gap:&lt;/b&gt; the booking confirmation and the clinical readiness decision are separate records [W05-S01], so a confirmation can exist while the slot is still held. The visitor arrived on a booking confirmation while Intake saw held, and no source gives the exception review an owner or a time limit [W05-S03].&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What the trace cannot prove:&lt;/b&gt; the supplied trace shows no completed readiness decision before arrival, but absence from a trace does not establish that the decision never occurred [W05-S04]." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="172" width="1070" height="196" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sources" value="&lt;b&gt;3 · Evidence and model review&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;W05-S01 supports the Scheduling steps: record slot and preferences, the booking-details decision and both its branches, the readiness request, and the booking confirmation. W05-S02 supports the Clinical Operations steps: receive request, check room and clinician availability, the availability decision, record readiness, and retain held status with capacity review. W05-S03 supports the Intake steps: locate appointment and check readiness status, the ready decision, confirm support arrangements, exception review, and the handoff. W05-S04 supports the incident path only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Correction after checking the model against the records:&lt;/b&gt; I first drew the booking confirmation as the same step as the readiness decision. W05-S01 states they are separate records, so I split them, which is what makes the incident path legible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Carried forward:&lt;/b&gt; W04-S02 same-day capacity rule, W04-S01 for telling Scheduling's held slot apart from Intake's held arrival, and the W04-S03 support-preference and W04-S04 minimum-access constraints.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remaining uncertainty:&lt;/b&gt; who produces the clarification Intake waits on and within what time; and whether a readiness decision occurred but was not captured in the supplied trace. Resolving these needs the readiness record owner in Clinical Operations and the full appointment record rather than the trace alone. No stakeholder has reviewed or approved this model." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="376" width="1070" height="196" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="reflection" value="&lt;b&gt;4 · Learning reflection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Mapping the current process made clear that a booking confirmation and a clinical readiness decision are two separate records, so an appointment can look confirmed to a visitor while Intake still sees it as held [W05-S01, W05-S03]. The handoff that is unclear is the one into Intake: when the status shows held, Dana opens an exception review with Scheduling and Clinical Operations, but no source names who produces the clarification or how long it should take [W05-S03]. The incident trace shows no completed readiness decision before the visitor arrived, although absence from the trace does not prove the decision never happened [W05-S04]. Week 4 asked what the clinic needs, written as testable requirements; this week asked who does what, in what order, and where the work stalls. Drawing the lanes exposed a gap that the requirements list by itself did not show." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fillColor=#fff7ee;strokeColor=#95694b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="580" width="1070" height="134" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="evidence" value="&lt;b&gt;5 · Portfolio evidence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Editable model: Week05/Artifact/Le_Matthew_CIT140_Week05_As_Is_Process_Model.drawio&lt;br&gt;Exported model: Week05/Artifact/Le_Matthew_CIT140_Week05_As_Is_Process_Model.pdf (both pages)&lt;br&gt;Discord evidence: Week05/Evidence/Week05_Discord_Post.png&lt;br&gt;Receipt: Week05/Receipt/Week05_Mission_Receipt.pdf" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=10;fillColor=#edf5f2;strokeColor=#5a7c7d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="722" width="1070" height="86" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
